dayz-server-operator (0.8.2-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Web interface: htmx 2.0.4, Leaflet 1.7.1, Fork Awesome 1.2.0 and the
    country flags are compiled into the binary; dzo no longer depends on
    libjs-htmx, libjs-leaflet, fonts-fork-awesome and iso-flags-svg, and
    web.assets and web.flags_dir default to none (the built-in copies)
    and only override them file by file.
  * The apt repository also publishes the suite "stable" (a symlink to
    trixie) and the installation guide uses it; "trixie" keeps working.
    CI install-tests the package in a clean Ubuntu 26.04 LTS container,
    blocking, next to Debian 13.
  * The package no longer depends on libjs-sphinxdoc: the HTML
    documentation ships Sphinx's own JavaScript and CSS instead of
    symlinks into /usr/share/javascript/sphinxdoc, so a package built on
    Debian 13 installs on Ubuntu 26.04 LTS whatever Sphinx version
    built it.
  * The post-install steps (data directory, subuid/subgid range,
    lingering, and the unit refresh and service restarts on upgrade)
    move into /usr/libexec/dzo/postinst, the one script the rpm and Arch
    packages will call too. The subordinate id range is no longer fixed
    at 100000-165535: it is the lowest free 65536-id block at or above
    100000 that overlaps no range in /etc/subuid and /etc/subgid, so the
    package installs on a host where another rootless podman user
    already holds that range. An existing range for dayz is kept.
  * On a host without a steamcmd package (Fedora, RHEL, Arch), dzo runs
    steamcmd from the localhost/dzo-steamcmd image that dzo setup builds:
    --steamcmd (dzo mod add/update/refresh, dzo product install/update) and
    dzo steam login --command default to /usr/libexec/dzo/steamcmd-container
    when PATH has no steamcmd. The wrapper mounts the steamcmd home under
    paths.secrets/steamcmd-home (created 0700) and paths.cache into the
    image at the same paths, so downloads and the Steam session persist; the
    new `dzo config get <paths.* key>` prints those resolved paths. dzo setup
    reports which steamcmd the downloads use.
  * Packages for Fedora 43 and later and the RHEL 10 family (rpm) and, best
    effort, for Arch Linux, built from the same binary and the same payload
    as the .deb, each with a signed repository next to the apt one (dnf and
    pacman); all three repositories are signed with the same key.
  * README and the documentation now show which distributions dzo supports
    and how well each is tested: Debian 13 is the reference, Ubuntu 26.04
    LTS, Fedora 43/44 and the RHEL 10 family are supported (blocking CI
    install jobs plus a manual release checklist on a VM), Arch, Ubuntu
    interim releases and Debian testing are best effort. They also say what
    is not verified yet: SELinux in enforcing mode on Fedora and the RHEL
    family, a real Steam login through the steamcmd container wrapper, and
    no btrfs snapshot backups on the RHEL 10 family.
  * dzo also ships as a container image (ghcr.io/bzed/dzo, tagged with the
    package version and latest): Debian trixie with systemd as PID 1, dayz
    at UID/GID 1000 with lingering, dzo's apt repository, and podman switched
    to remote against the host's user socket, so the game servers run on the
    host and survive a restart, update or replacement of the appliance. CI
    builds it from the .deb of the same run, boots it, and rebuilds it weekly
    for Debian security updates.
  * Running dzo as a container appliance is documented in docs/container.rst:
    the host requirements (rootless podman 5.4 or newer with systemd,
    podman.socket, lingering, systemd cgroups, btrfs for backups), the host
    user's quadlet and the dzo wrapper in contrib/appliance/, the same-path
    rule for the data directory, the three checks dzo setup makes in
    podman.mode remote, and what differs from a native install. The quadlet
    brings a crashed appliance back (Restart=on-failure) and waits longer
    than podman's own stop timeout (TimeoutStopSec=150) so the servers stop
    cleanly.

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bernd@bzed.de>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:04:18 +0100

dayz-server-operator (0.8.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dzo-admin 0.8.1, which changes the packaged PBO: a moved or spawned
    vehicle goes on top of the highest surface at the point (road, rock or
    roof) instead of at the terrain height, where it could end up inside
    the object, be thrown out or fall through the world and be deleted.
    Boats stay on the water.

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bernd@bzed.de>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 10:40:29 +0100

dayz-server-operator (0.8.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: dzo binary, config.yaml conffile, dayz system
    user via sysusers.d/tmpfiles.d, subuid/subgid + linger setup in
    postinst. No instance management commands ship yet (Phase 1 is
    still in progress); see IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.
  * Web users and logins. BREAKING for existing dzo web setups (see
    docs/migration.rst): web.backends and web.user_header are removed and
    refused (one web interface serves one installation, web.api reaches
    another host); the web interface needs serve.web_url, a token made with
    `dzo token create web --role admin --web` (the old delegate token no
    longer gives it anything) and a first admin from `dzo user grant --username <name>`.
    People are identified by Steam ID, log in with a password or Steam plus
    a second factor (TOTP, passkey or recovery code) and have a role per
    instance; dzo serve enforces it per instance, the audit log names the
    person and the browser address (expiring after
    serve.audit_ip_retention_days, default 90). New commands dzo user ...,
    new schema migration 0004 in the ban database, new keys serve.tls,
    serve.web_url, serve.login.*, serve.audit_ip_retention_days, web.tls,
    web.api, web.trusted_proxies. serve and web can speak HTTPS from
    certificate files that reload on change. dzo-web.service gains
    ExecReload; run `dzo units sync`. New dependencies:
    golang.org/x/crypto (argon2id), github.com/go-webauthn/webauthn,
    rsc.io/qr.
  * Player bans with evidence (dzo ban, dzo evidence, web UI, API);
    new dependency modernc.org/sqlite (pure Go, statically linked).
  * Player actions: kick with a reason (BattlEye), heal, fix gear and kill
    (dzo-admin 0.2.0, which changes the packaged PBO), in the API, the CLI
    and the web player panel. New permissions player.kick, player.kill,
    player.heal, player.fixgear.
  * IP addresses are personal data: player.ip (operator) shows the current
    address, ip.history (admin) the stored ones; bans and evidence carry
    opaque references instead. New config keys serve.ip_retention_days
    (default 90) and serve.vacuum_days (default 7); the ban database
    schema gains migration 0002.
  * Country flags in the player list; the player info shows the country,
    and with player.ip the city, approximate location and autonomous
    system. GeoLite2 .mmdb files (geoipupdate, /var/lib/GeoIP) give all of
    it, the legacy GeoIP.dat/GeoIPv6.dat of geoip-database (/usr/share/GeoIP)
    the country only and are the fallback. New dependency
    github.com/oschwald/geoip2-golang/v2 (ISC); new Depends:
    geoip-database, iso-flags-svg; new config keys serve.geoip_dir,
    serve.geoip_legacy_dir and web.flags_dir; new API route
    .../players/{steamid}/geo and a country field in the player list.
  * servermods.lock pins the servermod commits and PBO hashes; CI checks it.
  * The web interface ships a helicopter icon (Font Awesome Free 6.7.2,
    CC BY 4.0) that fonts-fork-awesome lacks; debian/copyright lists it.
  * Message ways: dzo player msg, the API and the web interface send by
    chat colour, on-screen notification, DayZ Expansion notification
    (six types) or RCon say; dzo-admin 0.3.0 (the packaged PBO changes)
    reports Expansion in its hello. New restarts.announce.ways and
    updates.restart_announce.ways: the countdown uses on-screen
    notifications once a minute in the last ten minutes by default, with
    RCon say as the fallback (API token: $DZO_TOKEN or announce.token,
    which dzo instance apply and dzo units sync create with the
    announcer role when an instance runs dzo-admin).
  * Map: territory flags (flag icon, time until the flag goes down) and,
    with DayZ Expansion, territory circles with the territory name, for
    operators; dzo-admin 0.4.0 (the packaged PBO changes). Operators can
    raise a flag from the map (new permission flag.raise, dzo flag raise,
    POST /instances/<i>/flags/<id>/raise).
  * Event feed: dzo-admin 0.5.0 reports kills (Expansion AI too), deaths,
    joins and leaves, base building and raids, flags and stashes; dzo adds
    in-game chat (BattlEye RCon) and admin actions. The newest 1000 events
    per instance are kept in <paths.db>/feed/<instance>.jsonl. GET
    /instances/<i>/feed, stream?only=feed, a live events page with a chat
    input in the web interface, dzo events [-f] on the console, and a Discord
    killfeed (instance.yaml killfeed, with an optional delay for PvP servers;
    Discord posts no longer ping anyone). The notifier gets a 10 second HTTP
    timeout.
  * Web interface: an instance switcher and an instance bar on every page,
    world, time, uptime, restart and mod version on the dashboard, a fixed
    teleport drag on the map, and a player database (Players page, API
    /players, permission player.history) with BattlEye global bans (asked
    from BattlEye's master server, per game) and Steam bans (optional Web API
    key, steam.web_api_key_file). New options steam.profile_lookup,
    steam.web_api_key_file and serve.session_retention_days.
  * Map: rebuilt houses and wells with the time until decay wears them down,
    the tunnel entrances (with and without a usable rope ladder) and an active
    sandstorm; dzo-admin 0.6.1 (the packaged PBO changes).
  * Killfeed: an Expansion AI is shown with its own name and its faction,
    AI "Frida" (West); the faction is no longer a raw stringtable key.
  * Move vehicles (drag on the map, "Move to coordinates", dzo vehicle move,
    POST /vehicles/<id>/move) to pull stuck ones out. A vehicle with players
    inside moves at most admin.move_occupied_max metres (new option, default
    200) and everyone takes no damage for 3 s; dzo-admin 0.7.0 (the packaged
    PBO changes).
  * Boats (vanilla and DayZ Expansion) are listed on the map and in the vehicle
    list as kind boat and can be spawned on the water, repaired, flipped, moved
    and deleted like cars; dzo-admin 0.7.0.
  * Last driver of vehicles: dzo-admin 0.8.0 reports who last took the
    driver's seat of each car, motorbike and boat (hello feature driver),
    and dzo serve keeps one record per vehicle in dzo.sqlite (forgotten
    admin.vehicle_forget_days after it is gone, new option, default 7). The
    vehicle list in the web interface and the API shows the last driver and
    the last drive, and each vehicle links to its place on the map.
  * Cleanup of unused vehicles: a previewed bulk delete of the vehicles nobody
    has driven for a number of days (web interface and API); occupied and
    covered vehicles are skipped, each delete is audited and the deletes the
    mod has not answered yet are listed as pending.
  * Database backup: serve.db_backup_hours and serve.db_backup_keep (new
    options) make regular consistent copies of dzo.sqlite, passed to the
    post_backup hooks as extra.db_backup.
  * A reload drops the hubs of instances removed from the site, and the hub
    forgets finished commands after 10 minutes (GET of an older command id
    answers 404).
  * BREAKING: dzo-admin 0.8.0 needs DayZ 1.30; servers still on DayZ 1.29
    have to stay on dzo-admin 0.7.x.

